## Summary

The `initials` field needed to appear on the Owner JSON response (`$.initials` → `"J.S."` for firstName `john`, lastName `smith`). Following the exact pattern already used for `displayName`, I made two small changes:

1. **`Person.java`** — added a `getInitials()` transient method alongside the existing `getDisplayName()`. Since `Owner` extends `Person`, both entities inherit it, and it lives on the domain object where name-derived formatting belongs:
   ```java
   @Transient
   public String getInitials() {
       return Character.toUpperCase(this.firstName.charAt(0)) + "."
           + Character.toUpperCase(this.lastName.charAt(0)) + ".";
   }
   ```

2. **`openapi.yml`** — added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, mirroring `displayName`. The code generator produces the DTO field and MapStruct auto-maps it from `getInitials()` (same convention that already wires up `displayName`), so no mapper changes were required.

No new class or catch-all was introduced — the logic reuses the established transient-getter + read-only-schema-property pattern.

